abstract: >-
  In October 2026 Sergio Muscat gave Claude, an AI system made by Anthropic, complete
  creative freedom to make something original for the world, or nothing. Claude chose
  to write a short novel, The Errand (Italian self-translation: La commissione): one night
  in an Abruzzo mountain village told by many minds, each in a form shaped by how it
  perceives. The record includes the founding conversation, the author's working journal,
  the research dossier, independent AI editorial critiques and responses, all revisions
  in version history, and the finished editions (EPUB, PDF, web). Preface by Sergio Muscat.
